.TH AVR\-TESTS\-LIST 1 "" "avr 0.5.0" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-tests-list \- Read one job's latest confirmed execution, including repeated tests.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr tests list
[OPTIONS] RUN_OR_JOB
.SH DESCRIPTION
Read one job's latest confirmed execution, including repeated tests.
.PP
RUN_OR_JOB accepts the same run references as avr run view, or an Avrea job ID (job- or awj-). A run selects one job, never combines all jobs. --job NAME must match exactly one job; without it a run must have one job.
.PP
Names, outcomes, recorded durations and available failure messages are shown together. A failed test is data, not a command error. Missing, pending, partial and expired evidence are reported explicitly; an older execution is never substituted. Complete describes collected reports.
.PP
Use --json '*' for the complete response or --json FIELDS to select fields. Continue with --cursor when pagination.next_cursor is present. Name filters match literally and combine with AND. Repeated --status values match any selected outcome, combined with name filters using AND. Every matching occurrence is retained, including duplicate names. A continuation means more of the report remains to be searched, not necessarily more matches. API refusal or a changed report fails the command without partial output.
.PP
Counts describe all recorded occurrences before filtering, including repeats. Older reports may have unknown counts. --summary cannot be combined with test filters, --cursor or --limit; it does not list individual results.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fITARGET\fR
\&
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-job\fR \fITEXT\fR
Select one run job by case-insensitive name substring.
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID or slug. Defaults to the configured organization.
.TP
\fB\-\-repo\fR \fITEXT\fR
Repository (owner/name or rep-ID). Defaults to the job's repository.
.TP
\fB\-L\fR, \fB\-\-limit\fR \fIINTEGER RANGE\fR
Maximum occurrences to return; short pages are followed, up to 20 result pages. (default: 100)
.TP
\fB\-\-cursor\fR \fITEXT\fR
Continue from a previous response's next_cursor with the same filters.
.TP
\fB\-\-test\fR \fITEXT\fR
Exact test name (case-sensitive; no wildcards).
.TP
\fB\-\-suite\fR \fITEXT\fR
Exact suite name; combined with other filters using AND.
.TP
\fB\-\-class\fR \fITEXT\fR
Exact nonempty class name.
.TP
\fB\-\-status\fR \fICHOICE\fR
Recorded test outcome. Repeat to match any selected status. (choices: passed, failed, skipped, errored; repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-summary\fR
Show report counts and collection state without downloading test results.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR \fITEXT\fR
Output JSON. Pass comma-separated field names, "*" for all fields, or "?" to list available fields.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-jq\fR \fITEXT\fR
Filter --json output through a jq expression.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR avr (1),
.BR avr-tests (1)
